`@theme`-declared variables are used to create utilities/variants, while plain `:root` variables are not automatically tied to utilities【/Users/davis/Developer/highmatter/grep-bench/.pi-bench/workspaces/2026-05-03T01-13-03-275Z/repos/tailwindcss/src/docs/theme.mdx:18-21】【/Users/davis/Developer/highmatter/grep-bench/.pi-bench/workspaces/2026-05-03T01-13-03-275Z/repos/tailwindcss/src/docs/theme.mdx:56-60】.

**How mapping works (v4):**
- Theme vars are defined in namespaces like `--color-*`, `--font-*`, etc. Each namespace maps to specific utility APIs【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:129-133】.
- The token name becomes part of the utility name (for examples: `--font-poppins` → `font-poppins`)【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:83-91】【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:95-99】.
- Some namespaces also create variants instead of (or in addition to) normal utilities, e.g. `--breakpoint-*` → `sm:*`, `3xl:*` style variants【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:103-118】【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:195-199】.

**At least 3 namespaces + what they generate:**
1. `--color-*` → color utilities (`bg-*`, `text-*`, `fill-*`)【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:147-151】  
2. `--font-*` → font-family utilities (`font-sans`, `font-poppins`)【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:155-159】【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:83-99】  
3. `--text-*` → font-size utilities (`text-xl`, `text-tiny`)【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:163-167】  
4. `--spacing-*` → spacing/sizing utilities (`px-*`, `max-h-*`)【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:211-215】  
5. `--breakpoint-*` → responsive variants (`sm:*`, `3xl:*`)【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:195-199】【.../src/docs/theme.mdx:117-123】

