## Tailwind CSS v4 Custom Utilities with @utility

Based on the Tailwind CSS v4 documentation, here are examples of custom utilities and how variants apply to them:

### 1. Simple Custom Utility

```css
/* [!code filename:CSS] */
@utility content-auto {
  content-visibility: auto;
}
```

**HTML usage:**
```html
<div class="content-auto"><!-- ... --></div>
```

### 2. Functional Custom Utility

```css
/* [!code filename:CSS] */
@utility tab-* {
  /* prettier-ignore */
  tab-size: --value(--tab-size-*);
}
```

With theme values:
```css
@theme {
  --tab-size-2: 2;
  --tab-size-4: 4;
}
```

This creates utilities like `tab-2` and `tab-4`.

### 3. How Variants Apply to Custom Utilities

Custom utilities **automatically support all Tailwind variants** (hover, focus, responsive, etc.) without additional configuration:

- **`hover:` and `focus:` variants** work immediately: `hover:content-auto`, `focus:tab-4`
- **`md:` and responsive variants** work immediately: `md:content-auto`, `lg:tab-4`

Both are applied because custom utilities are automatically inserted into the `utilities` layer alongside built-in utilities, which inherits full variant support.

### 4. Concrete CSS+HTML Example

```css
/* [!code filename:app.css] */
@utility scrollbar-thin {
  scrollbar-width: thin;
}

@utility shadow-soft-* {
  box-shadow: --value(--shadow-soft-*);
}

@theme {
  --shadow-soft-sm: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
  --shadow-soft-lg: 0 10px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}
```

```html
<!-- [!code filename:HTML] -->
<!-- Works with hover and md: variants -->
<div class="scrollbar-thin md:scrollbar-thin hover:shadow-soft-lg shadow-soft-sm">
  Content with thin scrollbar, soft shadow that enlarges on hover, and responsive behavior at md breakpoint
</div>
```

**Key points:**
- `hover:shadow-soft-lg` — hover variant applied to custom functional utility
- `md:scrollbar-thin` — responsive variant applied to custom simple utility  
- All variants work automatically; no special configuration needed

