## `+page.ts` vs `+page.server.ts`

| Topic | `+page.ts` (`PageLoad`) | `+page.server.ts` (`PageServerLoad`) |
|---|---|---|
| Where it runs | Server during SSR, then browser during hydration and later client-side navigations; if `export const ssr = false`, only in the browser | Always on the server |
| Extra access | No server-only extras | `clientAddress`, `cookies`, `locals`, `platform`, `request` via `ServerLoadEvent` |
| What it can do that the other cannot | Return any values, including custom classes and component constructors | Access DB/filesystem/private env vars; read/set cookies |
| Serialization | Not constrained the same way in docs | Must return data serializable with `devalue` |

## Serialization / `devalue`
From `content/docs/kit/20-core-concepts/20-load.md` and `content/blog/2023-02-21-streaming-snapshots-sveltekit.md`:

- Server load return values must be serializable with `devalue`.
- Supported examples listed in docs: JSON plus `BigInt`, `Date`, `Map`, `Set`, `RegExp`, repeated/cyclical references.
- Promises are allowed in returned data and can stream to the browser.
- If you need custom types, use transport hooks.
- The blog post also notes that `devalue` is used to serialize server-load data and `devalue.parse` is used on client-side navigation.

