In Tailwind CSS v4, `@theme` defines **theme variables**: special CSS variables that “influence which utility classes exist” in your project. Unlike variables in `:root`, variables in `@theme` map directly to Tailwind’s utility/variant APIs.

For example, defining:

```css
@theme {
  --color-mint-500: oklch(0.72 0.11 178);
}
```

makes utilities like `bg-mint-500`, `text-mint-500`, and `fill-mint-500` available.

Theme variables are grouped by namespace. Examples from the docs:

| `@theme` namespace | Generated utilities / variants |
|---|---|
| `--color-*` | Color utilities like `bg-red-500`, `text-sky-300`, plus related color utilities |
| `--font-*` | Font family utilities like `font-sans`; e.g. `--font-poppins` generates `font-poppins` |
| `--text-*` | Font size utilities like `text-xl` |
| `--spacing-*` | Spacing and sizing utilities like `px-4`, `max-h-16`, and many more |
| `--radius-*` | Border radius utilities like `rounded-sm` |
| `--shadow-*` | Box shadow utilities like `shadow-md` |
| `--breakpoint-*` | Responsive variants like `sm:*`; e.g. `--breakpoint-3xl` enables `3xl:*` |

Minimal example:

```css
/* app.css */
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --color-mint-500: oklch(0.72 0.11 178);
  --font-poppins: Poppins, sans-serif;
  --spacing-card: 2rem;
}
```

```html
<div class="bg-mint-500 p-card font-poppins">
  Custom theme utilities
</div>
```

Here:

- `--color-mint-500` enables `bg-mint-500` and other color utilities.
- `--font-poppins` enables `font-poppins`.
- `--spacing-card` enables spacing/sizing utilities using `card`, such as `p-card`.

